From 0f112f59b6be9b14115ddee088204e41f6e3df31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:03:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: trailer-exemptions.json rows for the 63 --strict
 offenders under the shipped engine c23bd8cc5

The export rehearsal counted 42 offenders under c23bd8cc5e (the hard no-provenance class only).
The tool's own predicates find 63: 42 no-provenance (39 also without Measured-effect), 12
loose-only and 9 without Measured-effect. 18 of the 21 soft rows are the r86i export's own
exemption rows, which never reached the fork; they are re-keyed here by exact subject match inside
c23bd8cc5e's ancestry with their text unchanged (old key kept in sha_r86i_export). The other 3
are the W1-collision commits 4eed112ad, ba3683034 and f2b078a88 (no Measured-effect).

Every row is an ancestor of the engine of record arifi-b11178-x1i-c23bd8cc5, so the only repair
would be an amend of built, served and tagged history. Each no-provenance row records its origin
(ArifiLabs native, with the lane); all 42 are fork-authored. Rows are keyed by full fork sha, so
the export re-key (rekey4.py) carries them through the commit-map. Commits after c23bd8cc5e are
repaired by a reword at the merge freeze, never exempted here.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Origin: release-prep (HQ82)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - ledger only; no inference code path is touched. Offender classes on release/prep (tool predicates, classify.py): before 63 x1i rows unexempted, after 63/63 EXEMPT; 58 post-x1i remain for the reword.
